name 'ai-and-algorithmic-decisions-postassessment-q12_2025'

question 'A shopping app offers free shipping only if your order total is over $50 and you\'re logged into your account. Which kind of logic makes that rule work correctly?'

right 'An AND operator that checks both the total amount and login status before applying free shipping'
wrong 'An OR operator that gives free shipping if either condition is true'
wrong 'A loop that adds more items until the order reaches $50 automatically'
wrong 'A variable that always sets shipping cost to $0, no matter the conditions'

allow_multiple_attempts true

